// Every string of Data Overflow's screens (docs/SURVIVAL.md 9.7), one table.
// DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(id, "text"): UTF-8, `|` breaks a line as in the game's
// own texts, `%s` / `%d` are filled by the screens. Only the glyphs the
// game's own texts use (9.1: ASCII and the item / element glyphs, the
// arrows, the Greek grades); T9 (tests/overflow_text_tests.cpp) checks every
// string against the game font's character list. The weapon, core, board,
// chip and technique names of a run are the game's own (the DB's NAME
// columns) and come from the director.

// The NPC (3.1, 3.4).
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(npc_name, "Gekomon")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_1, "Hello there! I keep the battle|simulator of the Digital Security|Guard.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_2, "It copies enemy data from the|servers and lets it pour in until|the simulator overflows.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_3, "We call it Data Overflow! Nothing|you win in there comes out with|you...")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_4, "...except your records, and the|Sim Bits the simulator pays you.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_5, "Your Digimon fights on its own in|there. Just keep it moving and|survive as long as you can!")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(intro_6, "Oh, and if you meet any Gekomon|in there... those are copies. I|am the original. Probably.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(ask, "What will you do?")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(choice_enter, "Enter the simulator")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(choice_plug_lab, "Plug Lab")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(choice_records, "Data Records")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(choice_help, "How does it work?")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(choice_leave, "Never mind")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(goodbye, "Come back any time!")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(crowd, "The simulator only takes one|Digimon at a time. Come back on|your own!")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(back_time, "Welcome back! You lasted %s.|Not bad at all!")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(back_clear, "Welcome back! Simulation|complete! You beat the whole|thing!")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(back_gekomon, "Welcome back! Beaten by a|Gekomon? I will pretend I did|not see that.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(back_time_up, "Welcome back! Time ran out on|LordKnightmon, but you got that|far. Not bad at all!")

// How does it work? (3.4: four pages: controls, the weapon ladder,
// techniques, gear).
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(help_1, "Move with the stick: your Digimon|strikes on its own. A uses a|disk, L opens the disk panel.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(help_2, "Every hit grows the Art's skill.|Past a weapon's skill points the|next weapon of the ladder comes.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(help_3, "Your Digimon's own six techniques|come with levels and skill, and|fire on their own cooldowns.")
DW4_OVERFLOW_TEXT(help_4, "Each level-up offers three picks:|a Forge, Training, a Core, a|Board, a chip or a Plug.")

